From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 13:04:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 119/119] Typing in the Markdown preview switches to Source

A Markdown file opens in Preview, which is read-only, so the first keys
a user typed were lost. Now a key with text (letters, digits, space,
punctuation, also with Shift, AltGr or a dead key) or Enter, typed
without Ctrl, Alt or Super, switches the tab to Source (as Ctrl+Shift+V
does) and goes in there: at the end of the block at the top of the
preview, with the editor scrolled to show it. A heading and a list item
are blocks of their own; a paragraph runs on over lines that cannot
interrupt it, as in CommonMark. In a code block the text goes at the
end of the code, never on a fence. Enter continues a table or list as
in the editor. Keys typed before the editor has focus follow at the
cursor, Backspace, Delete and Tab included.

Arrows, Page Up/Down, Home/End and shortcuts work in Preview as before.
In Vim mode keys are commands, so nothing changes there. Keys never
edit the document while a menu, a context menu, a dialog, a prompt or
the settings are open: typing with the Edit menu open used to edit the
text behind it and crash libcosmic's menu layout.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

